window.MONSTER_CHUNK_128 = [{"name":"Death's Head Inphidian","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"NE","size":"Medium","type":"monstrous humanoid","subtypes":["reptilian"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":21,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":18,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +8 natural","hp":68,"hd":"8d10+24","hdvalue":8,"fort":7,"ref":9,"will":0,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"quarterstaff +12 (1d6+4 plus poison or grab) or 2 snake-hands +13 (1d8+4 plus bleed and poison)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"bleed","details":"1d4"},{"type":"death's head staff"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":8,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":11,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"speak with snakes","details":"as speak with animals, but snakes only"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"accelerate poison"},{"spell":"snake staff"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"cause fear"},{"spell":"suggestion"}]}],"strength":18,"dexterity":17,"constitution":17,"intelligence":19,"wisdom":20,"charisma":18,"baseatk":8,"cmb":1,"cmd":14,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (snake-hands)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":7},{"skill":"Bluff","value":8},{"skill":"Climb","value":11},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":12},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":15},{"skill":"Knowledge (history)","value":8},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":11},{"skill":"Perception","value":16},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":9},{"skill":"Stealth","value":14},{"skill":"Survival","value":16}],"languages":["Common","Inphidian","Sylvan","Undercommon","speak with snakes"],"sq":[{"type":"snake empathy"}],"environments":["any underground","warm forests","warm plains"],"organizations":["band (1 death's head inphidian plus 1-2 rattler inphidians)","troupe (1 death's head inphidian plus 1 night adder inphidian, 1-2 rattler inphidians, and 3-4 giant vipers)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This tall slender humanoid is dressed in dark-colored robes. Its body is covered in dull blue-green scales with whorls of reddish-brown. Its head is viper-like and its arms end in snake-like hands. It clutches a long wooden staff tipped with a ruby-encrusted snake's skull.","group":"Inphidian","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Bite-injury; save DC 21 Fort; frequency 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d4 Con damage; cure 2 consecutive saves. The save DC is Constitution-based and includes a +4 racial bonus."},{"type":"Snake Empathy","kind":"Ex","details":"Snakes, including giant snakes, don't willingly attack a death's head inphidian, though they can be forced to do so by magic. If the death's head inphidian attacks a snake, its protection against that creature ends."},{"type":"Death's Head Staff","kind":"Ex","details":"The staff of a death's head inphidian can hold poisons in a specially crafted chamber inside the jewel encrusted snake skull. The chamber holds enough poison to deliver three doses. Most death's head inphidians fill the chamber with their own poison (use the stats above). In lieu of poisoning an opponent struck by the staff, a death's head can command its staff to grapple and constrict its target. When a foe is successfully hit by the staff, the death's head inphidian can make an immediate grapple check as a free action. If successful, the opponent is pinned and takes 1d6+6 points of bludgeoning damage each round until it escapes. (Use the death's head inphidian's statistics above to resolve the grapple and escape.) This staff functions only in the hands of a death's head inphidian. In the hands of any other creature, it acts as a normal quarterstaff. The gem-encrusted snake skull is worth a total of 1,000-3,000 gp."}],"description":"Death's head inphidians may not be the strongest or largest of the inphidian races, but they certainly are the most feared and respected; hence the reason the death's head is the leader of an inphidian nest. These creatures rule by fear and maintain tight control over their nest. Rules, commands, judgments, and punishments are all meted out by a death's head and all come quickly. As a death's head ages and draws near the end of its life, its position is often challenged by other death's heads, all vying for control of the inphidian nest. Such challenges generally end in the death of all but one death's head inphidian, who becomes the new leader of the nest, after the current leader dies (which is often times aided by the death's head in waiting). For this reason, as a death's head ages, it is rarely ever encountered alone, always having a retinue of other inphidians or giant snakes around it at all times.\n\nA typical death's head inphidian stands 6 ft. tall and weighs 180 pounds. Its dull blue-green scales darken and fade as it ages. A death's head has an average lifespan of 50 years.\n\nA death's head in combat is a fearsome creature, having many tools at its disposal-and it uses all of them to the best of its ability. It usually opens combat with its spell-like abilities (suggestion or cause fear) and then launches into melee with its snake hands and staff. A poisoned foe is subjected to its accelerated poison spell-like ability. If overwhelmed, a death's head uses its snake staff ability to occupy its opponents while it makes its escape.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Demonic Mist","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"CE","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["chaotic","evil","extraplanar"],"init":9,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":16,"ac_touch":16,"ac_flat_footed":10,"ac_mods":"+5 Dex, +1 dodge","hp":47,"hd":"5d10+20","hdvalue":5,"fort":8,"ref":9,"will":20,"defensive_abilities":["amorphous"],"dr":"5/ magic","immunities":["acid","cold"],"resists":[{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":16,"weaknesses":["vulnerability to wind"],"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":50,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"touch +10 (5d6)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"psychic crush"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":5,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":9,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"cause fear"},{"spell":"confusion"}]},{"frequency":"2/day","spells":[{"spell":"enervation"},{"spell":"vampiric touch"}]}],"dexterity":21,"constitution":18,"intelligence":11,"wisdom":13,"charisma":16,"baseatk":5,"cmb":26,"cmd":51,"feats":[{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":13},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":13},{"skill":"Fly","value":21},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":8},{"skill":"Perception","value":9},{"skill":"Stealth","value":13,"special":"+21 in fog or mist"}],"languages":["Abyssal","Common","telepathy 100 ft."],"sq":[{"type":"gaseous"}],"environments":["any (Abyss)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","gang (3-6)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This cloud of sickly green mist seems to move as if it were alive.","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Gaseous","kind":"Ex","details":"A demonic mist can pass through small holes, even cracks, without reducing its speed. It cannot enter water or other liquid. It has no Strength score, and cannot manipulate objects."},{"type":"Psychic Crush","kind":"Su","details":"Three times per day, as a standard action, a demonic mist can attempt to crush the mind of a single creature within 40 ft. The target must make a DC 15 Will save or take 3d6 points of damage and become sickened for 1d4+1 rounds. This is a mind-affecting effect. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Vulnerability to Wind","kind":"Ex","details":"A demonic mist is treated as a Tiny creature for the purposes of determining the effects high wind has upon it."}],"description":"Some scholars and sages believe a demonic mist is the incomplete manifestation of a demon on the Material Plane. Others conjecture it is a representation of chaos unleashed by the denizens of the Abyss. Whatever the true nature of its origin, a demonic mist is a creature wholly chaotic and evil. When encountered on the Material Plane it is most often in areas of consecrated ground such as graveyards, temples, and holy sites. In their native environment, demonic mists are found haunting the most putrid and disgusting of the Abyssal planes. Those planes covered with oozes, mires, fens, and swamps are favored by these creatures. Demonic mists have voracious appetites and always seem to be on the hunt. They are carnivorous creatures devouring just about anything they came across. Once a demonic mist slays its prey, it moves over the body and rapidly digests it, draining blood and body fluids, and leaving nothing more than a dried husk.\n\nA demonic mist's semi-solid body is composed of a strange, sickly green and ever-shifting mist. It can change its color to a semi-translucent whitish smoke, thereby blending in and hiding in areas of normal fog and mist. When hiding in this way, a demonic mist seeks to quickly close ground with its target and attack from ambush, unleashing its psychic crush and enervating attacks at the closest and strongest opponents.\n\nDemonic mists are often found in the employ of clerics dedicated to the demonic lords (particularly Tsathogga and Jubilex), serving as temple guards or assassins.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Devil Dog","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"CE","size":"Medium","type":"magical beast","subtypes":["cold"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"}],"auras":["frightful presence (30 ft., DC 13)"],"ac":15,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":13,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +3 natural","hp":45,"hd":"6d10+12","hdvalue":6,"fort":7,"ref":7,"will":10,"immunities":["cold"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to fire"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50}],"melee":"bite +9 (1d6+3 plus trip)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"throat-rip"}],"strength":15,"dexterity":15,"constitution":15,"intelligence":6,"wisdom":12,"charisma":10,"baseatk":6,"cmb":22,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":39,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":6},{"skill":"Stealth","value":7,"special":"+13 in snow and ice"},{"skill":"Survival","value":3,"special":"+7 tracking by scent"}],"environments":["any cold"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","pack (7-16)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature resembles a large wolf with frost white fur and glowing blue eyes.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Throat-Rip","kind":"Ex","details":"As a full-round action, a devil dog can deliver a coup de grace against a helpless opponent. If the victim survives the attack, he must succeed on a Fortitude save (DC 10 + damage dealt) or die. Opponents killed in this manner cannot be raised, but resurrection, true resurrection, or the like can restore the slain creature to life."}],"description":"The wolf-like devil dog may be an interbred species of wild dog and winter wolf. A devil dog is smaller than a winter wolf but much larger than nearly any normal dog of any breed - about 5 ft. long and 3 ft. high at the shoulder. A devil dog is white in color, blending in almost perfectly with its snowbound environment. Thanks to their appearance, devil dogs are often mistaken for winter wolves by inexperienced travelers in icy regions. Devil dog packs have been known to stalk and attack humanoids and other creatures much larger than the pack members. They are smart enough to use their coloration to their best advantage in the hunt.\n\nDevil dogs hunt in packs, using tactics similar to normal wild dogs and wolves: the pack circles the prey, with each dog taking its turn attacking.\n\nDevil dogs attempt to rip out the throat of any helpless opponent.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Devil Dog originally appeared in the First Edition Fiend Folio (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1981) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Dire Rat Megaswarm","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Small","type":"animal","subtypes":["megaswarm"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":14,"ac_touch":14,"ac_flat_footed":11,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +1 size","hp":52,"hd":"8d8+8 (+8)","hdvalue":8,"fort":9,"ref":9,"will":3,"defensive_abilities":["half damage from piercing weapons"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"climb","speed":20},{"type":"swim","speed":20}],"melee":"swarm (2d6 plus disease)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"0 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"disease"},{"type":"distraction","details":"DC 15"}],"strength":10,"dexterity":17,"constitution":13,"intelligence":2,"wisdom":13,"charisma":4,"baseatk":6,"cmb":-1,"cmd":12,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Toughness"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":11},{"skill":"Perception","value":11},{"skill":"Stealth","value":14},{"skill":"Swim","value":11}],"environments":["any urban"],"organizations":["solitary","pack (2-4 megaswarms)","infestation (7-12 megaswarms)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"A squirming horde of vicious rats the size of small dogs streams forward. They have coarse, spiky fur, feral eyes, and jagged, yellowed teeth. They surge ahead in a roiling mass of filth and stench.","group":"Megaswarm","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Disease","kind":"Ex","details":"Filth fever: Swarm-injury; save DC 15 Fort; onset 1d3 days; frequency 1/day; effect 1d3 Dex damage and 1d3 Con damage; cure 2 consecutive saves. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Megaswarm Traits","kind":"Ex","details":"Megaswarms are not so called because of the size of the swarm but rather the size of the creatures that compose the swarm. Unlike normal swarms, megaswarms are composed of Small creatures which are usually a megafauna version of a normal swarm and otherwise behave in a swarmlike manner. There are usually around 100 creatures in a megaswarm. The net effect is that they take only half damage from piercing weapons but take normal damage from other weapons. In addition when the swarm is reduced to 0 hit points or lower and breaks up, unless the damage was dealt by area-affecting attacks, then 2d6 surviving members of the megaswarm continue their attack, though now only as individual creatures. Otherwise, a megaswarm conforms to all of the other swarm traits."}],"description":"Much like a swarm of ordinary rats, a dire rat swarm is composed of a teeming mass of disease-ridden dire rats intent on feeding on whatever they can catch. A dire rat swarm usually exists in abandoned ruins or city dumps where there is a plentiful food supply and a lack of significant predators.\n\nA dire rat swarm seeks to overrun and attack any warm-blooded prey it encounters. It typically ignores undead and other creatures that are not warm-blooded.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"Original author Greg A. Vaughan  Originally appearing in Slumbering Tsar (© Frog God Games/ Greg A. Vaughan, 2012)"},{"name":"Drelb","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"NE","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["extraplanar","incorporeal","psionic"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":15,"ac_touch":15,"ac_flat_footed":12,"ac_mods":"+2 deflection, +3 Dex, +0 natural","hp":50,"hd":"6d10+12","hdvalue":6,"fort":6,"ref":8,"will":3,"defensive_abilities":["incorporeal"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"fly","speed":20,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"incorporeal touch +9 (1d4 plus nether chill)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"illusory retreat"}],"dexterity":16,"constitution":14,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":14,"charisma":15,"baseatk":6,"cmb":2,"cmd":12,"feats":[{"feat":"Ability Focus (nether chill)"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":11},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":11},{"skill":"Knowledge (the planes)","value":10},{"skill":"Perception","value":11},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":11},{"skill":"Stealth","value":12},{"skill":"Survival","value":11}],"languages":["Common","Daemonic"],"sq":[{"type":"psionic adaptation"}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This spectral figure is composed of darkness and has no discernible features except its eyes-two small pinpoints of light that burn with a hellish glow.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Illusory Retreat","kind":"Sp","details":"A drelb can rapidly diminish its form while it advances forward. To the onlooker, it appears as if the drelb is retreating. Creatures succeeding on a DC 20 Will save see through this illusion; otherwise, the drelb advances into melee range and its opponent is considered flat-footed for the drelb's next attack following the use of this ability. A creature that has seen a drelb use this ability before gains a +2 circumstance bonus on its Will save. The save DC is Charisma-based and includes a +5 racial bonus."},{"type":"Nether Chill","kind":"Su","details":"A living creature touched by a drelb must make a DC 17 Fortitude save or immediately drops anything it is holding and fall prone, shivering for 1 round. It isn't helpless but is unable to make any actions during this round. The save DC is Constitution-based and includes a +2 bonus for the drelb's Ability Focus feat."},{"type":"Psionic Adaptation","kind":"Su","details":"A drelb can imitate any psionic power or psi-like ability used within 30 ft. of it as a standard action. A drelb has a manifester level of 5th. The save DC (if any) to resist an imitated psionic power or psi-like ability is 12 + the level of the power. The save DC is Charisma-based. Further, any psionic power or psi-like ability that directly targets a drelb is reflected back on the attacker with full effect (manifester level and save DC equal to that of the original manifester)."}],"description":"Drelbs are energy creatures that make their home on the Negative Energy Plane. They are summoned to the Material Plane by evil spellcasters who task them with the duty of guarding treasure or secret places to be left alone. Hence, they are sometimes referred to as haunting custodians. A drelb resembles and is nearly indistinguishable from a wraith (DC 25 Perception check to notice the difference from a distance of 10 ft. or more). Drelbs are not undead and cannot be turned, though they sometimes feign being affected, using their illusory retreat ability to trick their opponents.\n\nA drelb attacks by touching an opponent with its incorporeal touch. It uses its illusory retreat ability at the first chance, attempting to catch an opponent unaware.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Drelb originally appeared in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Ectoplasm","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"ooze","subtypes":["incorporeal"],"init":1,"senses":[{"type":"blindsight","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":11,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":10,"ac_mods":"+1 deflection, +1 Dex, -1 size, +0 natural","hp":47,"hd":"5d8+25","hdvalue":5,"fort":6,"ref":2,"will":-4,"defensive_abilities":["incorporeal"],"immunities":["ooze traits"],"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":30,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"incorporeal touch +3 (1d8 Strength damage)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon"},{"type":"manifestation"},{"type":"Strength damage"},{"type":"undead bane"}],"dexterity":12,"constitution":21,"wisdom":1,"charisma":1,"baseatk":3,"cmb":5,"cmd":16,"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":7}],"sq":[{"type":"glow"}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature gives off light with the approximate brightness of a candle, and appears to be a shimmering cloud of filaments, tendrils, and whips of eerie mist. The form of the thing continuously roils and billows like a cloud, and it is eerily silent.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"Once every 2 rounds as a standard action, an ectoplasm can release a 20-foot cone of ectoplasmic goo at its foes. Affected opponents must succeed on a DC 17 Fortitude save or be affected as if by a sleep spell (caster level 7th). A successful save renders a creature immune to that ectoplasm's breath weapon for 24 hours. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Glow","kind":"Su","details":"An ectoplasm continually gives off light with the approximate brightness of a candle. It cannot consciously extinguish this light. When an ectoplasm is killed, this light fades to darkness."},{"type":"Manifestation","kind":"Su","details":"An ectoplasm dwells on the Ethereal Plane and as an ethereal creature, it cannot affect or be affected by anything in the material world. When an ectoplasm manifests, it partly enters the Material Plane and becomes visible but incorporeal. A manifested ectoplasm can be harmed only by other incorporeal creatures, magic weapons, or spells, with a 50% chance to ignore any damage from a corporeal source. A manifested ectoplasm can pass through solid objects at will, and its own attacks pass through armor. A manifested ectoplasm always moves silently."},{"type":"Strength Damage","kind":"Su","details":"The touch of an ectoplasm deals 1d8 points of Strength damage to living opponents."},{"type":"Undead Bane","kind":"Su","details":"Against corporeal undead, an ectoplasm deals 1d8 points of Strength damage and 1d8 points of damage. Ectoplasms ignore the damage reduction of corporeal undead."}],"description":"Many encounters with glowing, ghostly spheres can be attributed to ectoplasms rather than restless spirits. An ectoplasm, sometimes called a ghost ooze, is a faintly glowing orb of immaterial substance that lurks in catacombs and cemeteries. Although incorrectly assumed by most to be some form of incorporeal undead, ectoplasms are quite alive. Ectoplasms dwell in places of the dead because they consume dead flesh, slowly dissolving decaying bones and skin and absorbing the nutrients directly. The strange irony of the ectoplasm is that a cemetery ‘haunted' by these creatures is almost certain to be free of any corporeal undead; the ectoplasm makes a meal of them as soon as it discovers them. Ectoplasms are not undead and cannot be turned by clerics. Although its primary diet consists of the dead, an ectoplasm is also a threat to the living. An ectoplasm attacks anything within the range of its senses that disturbs it. An ectoplasm that encounters a living opponent attacks for a few rounds before attempting to escape-it senses that it can get no sustenance from the opponent. If it finds an undead opponent, an ectoplasm continues to attack until it or the opponent has been destroyed.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Fear Guard","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"CE","size":"Medium","type":"undead","subtypes":["incorporeal"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"see in darkness"}],"auras":["fear aura (20 ft., DC 17)"],"ac":17,"ac_touch":17,"ac_flat_footed":14,"ac_mods":"+4 deflection, +2 Dex, +1 dodge, +0 natural","hp":51,"hd":"6d8+24","hdvalue":6,"fort":6,"ref":4,"will":6,"defensive_abilities":["channel resistance +2","incorporeal"],"immunities":["undead traits"],"weaknesses":["daylight vulnerability"],"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":30,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"incorporeal touch +7 (1d3 Wis  damage)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"create spawn"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":8,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":8,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"darkness"},{"spell":"ray of enfeeblement"}]},{"frequency":"2/day","spells":[{"spell":"deeper darkness"}]}],"dexterity":15,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":12,"charisma":18,"baseatk":4,"cmb":6,"cmd":20,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (incorporeal touch)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":15},{"skill":"Perception","value":10},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":10},{"skill":"Stealth","value":10,"special":"+18 in dim light and darkness"}],"environments":["any underground"],"organizations":["solitary","group (2-5)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This incorporeal entity appears as a hooded humanoid figure clad in flowing robes of translucent gray over a suit of ghostly armor. Its facial features are a swirl of maddening images, fluctuating between a serene countenance and a face twisted into a grimace of horror and fear.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Create Spawn","kind":"Su","details":"Any living creature reduced to Wisdom 0 by a fear guard is slain and becomes a fear guard under the control of its killer in 1d6 rounds."},{"type":"Daylight Vulnerability","kind":"Ex","details":"A fear guard exposed to natural sunlight (not merely bright light) suffers 2d6 points of damage per round of exposure and is slowed (as the spell)."}],"description":"Fear guards embody evil in its blackest conjuration. They are summoned from some unknown place by evil wizards and clerics to guard prized possessions or a valued location.\n\nShrouding themselves in a preternatural darkness, fear guards fight using spell-like abilities and their incorporeal touch. If guarding a particular location, a fear guard fights until either it is slain or driven away, or its opponents are slain or flee. If exposed to natural sunlight, fear guards either surround themselves with magical darkness for protection or flee if this unsuccessful.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Fen Witch","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"CE","size":"Medium","type":"monstrous humanoid","init":1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["horrific appearance (60 ft., DC 15, 1d8 Str)"],"ac":14,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":13,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +3 natural","hp":39,"hd":"6d10+6","hdvalue":6,"fort":5,"ref":6,"will":7,"sr":15,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"2 claws +9 (1d4+1)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"death speak","details":"DC 15"},{"type":"mind probe","details":"Will DC 15"}],"strength":17,"dexterity":12,"constitution":13,"intelligence":14,"wisdom":14,"charisma":15,"baseatk":6,"cmb":9,"cmd":20,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":12},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":11},{"skill":"Perception","value":11},{"skill":"Stealth","value":10},{"skill":"Survival","value":10},{"skill":"Swim","value":12}],"languages":["Aklo","Common","telepathy 100 ft."],"sq":[{"type":"hag"},{"type":"swamp stride"}],"environments":["temperate swamps"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This creature appears as a female humanoid with one nostril, webbed ft. and hands, and fiery red eyes. Her body is cloaked in tattered robes of gray or brown. Her hands end in razor-sharp claws and her hair is usually long and unkempt.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Death Speak","kind":"Su","details":"A fen witch who knows an individual's true name can speak that name as a swift action. If the individual hears the fen witch speak its name, that creature must succeed on a DC 15 Will save or perish. If the save succeeds, that creature cannot be affected again by the same fen witch's death speak for 24 hours. Note that the fen witch doesn't need to speak a language the creature understands in order to affect it; she only needs to speak its true name. Other fen witches or creatures who hear the target's true name cannot use this ability; it only functions for the fen witch after she has used her mind probe ability on the target. The save DC is Charisma-based. Whether the fen witch's Death Speak ability is successful or not, the target's name remains fresh in her mind for 24 hours. After that, she must use her mind probe ability again to retrieve a creature's true name."},{"type":"Hag","kind":"Ex","details":"A fen witch counts as a hag for the purpose of joining a hag's coven."},{"type":"Horrific Appearance","kind":"Su","details":"The sight of a fen witch is so revolting that anyone within 60 ft. (other than another fen witch or hag) who sets eyes upon one must succeed on a DC 15 Fortitude save or instantly be weakened, taking 1d8 points of Strength damage. Creatures that are affected by this power or that successfully save against it cannot be affected again by the same fen witch's horrific appearance for 24 hours. This is a mind-affecting effect. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Mind Probe","kind":"Su","details":"As a full-round action, a fen witch can peer into the mind of a living creature within 60 ft. in an attempt to extract the creature's true name. The target can resist the mental trespassing by succeeding on a DC 15 Will save. If the save fails, the fen witch has learned the creature's true name and can use her death speak ability. Creatures with an Intelligence score of 2 or less and creatures with no Intelligence score are immune to this ability. Psionic creatures can use defense modes or other psionic abilities to counter this probe. A creature that successfully saves cannot be affected again by the same fen witch's mind probe for one day. The save DC is Wisdom-based."},{"type":"Swamp Stride","kind":"Ex","details":"A fen witch can move through any sort of natural difficult terrain at its normal speed while within a swamp. Magically altered terrain affects a fen witch normally."}],"description":"The fen witch is a creature of legend, found only in the most remote of places. It is a solitary creature and disdains all that invade its realm. A fen witch is thoroughly evil and malign, speaking to those she encounters only to learn the true name of one of the trespassers in her realm so she may utilize her power to slay that individual. Fen witches who take class levels usually advance as clerics, druids, sorcerers, or witches.\n\nFen witches rarely engage in combat, relying on their death speak ability to slay a creature almost instantaneously (and hopefully drive off the victim's comrades by instilling fear in any remaining creatures).\n\nFailing this, the fen witch prefers direct combat to subterfuge and attacks relentlessly.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Fire Eel","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"magical beast","subtypes":["aquatic"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":19,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +8 natural, -1 size","hp":51,"hd":"6d10+18","hdvalue":6,"fort":8,"ref":9,"will":4,"resists":[{"type":"fire","value":20}],"speed":[{"type":"swim","speed":40}],"melee":"bite +12 (2d6+9 plus grab)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"fire shroud"}],"strength":22,"dexterity":14,"constitution":16,"intelligence":2,"wisdom":14,"charisma":11,"baseatk":6,"cmb":13,"cmb_special":"+3 vs. grapple","cmd":25,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":10},{"skill":"Perception","value":7},{"skill":"Stealth","value":3},{"skill":"Swim","value":19}],"environments":["temperate oceans","warm oceans"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","nest (3-10)"],"treasure":"incidental","description_visual":"This eel is about 10 ft. long and roughly one foot thick. It has a broad, triangular head and dark gray scales.","group":"Eel","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Fire Shroud","kind":"Ex","details":"A fire eel constantly secretes highly flammable oil from its body. Upon contact with the air, the oil bursts into flames. The oil normally burns for 1 minute before extinguishing itself. Anyone contacting the burning oil takes 3d6 points of fire damage. Underwater, a fire eel can release this oil quickly (as a swift action) in a 10-foot radius around its body. The oil automatically ignites at the start of the fire eel's next turn. It deals the same fire damage as above, but only burns for 5 rounds underwater. A fire eel can ignite its oil once per minute in this way."}],"description":"Fire eels are a beautiful but dangerous species of aquatic beast that secrete and can ignite an oily residue on their skin to drive away predators and attract a mate. The flames emitted by a fire eel can be green, blue, red, or violet, or even a pattern of these colors, depending on the individual eel. Fire eels can be particularly dangerous to seagoing vessels during their mating season, when they come to the surface en masse to perform fiery courtship rituals, and are more aggressive than usual.\n\nFire eels are at home in both saltwater and freshwater, and live in groups of up to 10 eels. A fire eel lair consists of a number of long and winding tunnels burrowed into sand, rocks, or mud in shallow water. These tunnels eventually empty into a large central chamber. Fire eels, normally non-aggressive, become highly aggressive if their lair is threatened.\n\nFire eels are normally inoffensive, and avoid combat if possible. However, if they are attacked, grabbed, or if it is their mating season, they become more aggressive, and use their fire shroud to ward off attacks while they bite relentlessly until their opponents are driven away.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Fire Phantom","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"CE","size":"Medium","type":"undead","subtypes":["extraplanar","fire"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":16,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":14,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +6 natural, -2 rage","hp":38,"hd":"7d8 (+7)","hdvalue":7,"fort":4,"ref":4,"will":6,"defensive_abilities":["channel resistance +4"],"immunities":["fire","undead traits"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"2 slams +10 (1d4+4 plus 1d6 fire))","ranged":"fire blast +7 touch (2d6 fire)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"fire"},{"type":"fire blast"},{"type":"immolation"},{"type":"rage"}],"strength":19,"dexterity":14,"intelligence":5,"wisdom":12,"charisma":14,"baseatk":5,"cmb":9,"cmd":21,"feats":[{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (slam)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Intimidate","value":9},{"skill":"Perception","value":10}],"environments":["any (Elemental Plane of Fire)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This humanoid has raging fire for hair and flame-encased fists.  Elemental fire plays across its body exposing patches of charred flesh.  Its eyes and tongue look like tiny balls of molten fire. Blackened teeth fill its mouth and flames dance in the back of its throat.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Fire","kind":"Ex","details":"A fire phantom's fists are swathed in elemental fire. Any melee hit deals fire damage. Creatures attacking a fire phantom unarmed or with natural weapons take fire damage each time their attacks hit."},{"type":"Fire Blast","kind":"Su","details":"Once every 1d4 rounds, as a standard action, a fire phantom can hurl a small globe of elemental fire to a range of 30 ft. (no range increment). By making a successful ranged touch attack, it deals 2d6 points of fire damage. A creature hit must make a successful DC 15 Reflex save to avoid catching on fire. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Immolation","kind":"Su","details":"Normally used as a last resort, a fire phantom can detonate itself in an inferno of elemental fire that deals 6d6 points of fire damage to all creatures within a 10-foot radius. A successful DC 15 Reflex save halves the damage. The save DC is Charisma-based. This instantly kills the fire phantom if it fails a DC 20 Will save. Even if the fire phantom survives, its flames are extinguished for 1 minute. During this time the fire phantom cannot use its fire blast ability and cannot deal fire damage with its slam attack. It retains the fire subtype. After 1 minute, its fires relight and it may deal fire damage normally and use its fire blast ability. If the fire phantom survives the immolation it may not use it again for one day."},{"type":"Rage","kind":"Ex","details":"A fire phantom is in a constant state of agony from the elemental fire that consumes its body. Therefore, it is always in a berserk rage and gains Str +4 and -2 AC (both already included in the statistics block above). The fire phantom cannot end this rage voluntarily and it cannot be suppressed or negated."}],"description":"When a creature dies on the Elemental Plane of Fire, its soul often melds with part of the fiery plane and reforms as a fire phantom; a humanoid creature composed of rotted and burned flesh and elemental fire. Fire phantoms desire nothing more than to return to the Material Plane and destroy as many living creatures as possible by consuming them in the same flames that now house their spirit.\n\nFire phantoms are encountered in areas where fires are already burning (campfires, pyres, vigils, etc). They step through a portal from the Plane of Fire into a fire on the Material Plane. This fire must be at least Small or larger; else any attempt by the fire phantom to enter the Material Plane through that fire automatically fails. Once it enters the plane, it often lies in wait in the fire for potential victims to come near it. A fire phantom hiding inside a fire is difficult to see requiring DC 25 Perception check.\n\nA fire phantom waits inside its fire until it spots a living creature. It then rushes out, shrieking and hurling globes of fire. If faced with overwhelming odds or facing certain destruction, the fire phantom either moves as close as possible to as many foes as possible or attempts to draw in as many of its opponents as possible and uses it immolation ability.\n\nIn normal melee, the fire phantom alternates between hurling globes of fire and pummeling a foe with its burning fists. When a fire phantom is wounded, flames dance and play around the wound. Fire phantoms fight until destroyed or all opponents are dead or flee.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Fogwarden","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"NE","size":"Medium","type":"aberration","init":3,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["fear (30 ft., DC 14)"],"ac":16,"ac_touch":16,"ac_flat_footed":12,"ac_mods":"+2 deflection, +3 Dex, +1 dodge, +0 natural","hp":22,"hd":"4d8+4","hdvalue":4,"fort":2,"ref":4,"will":4,"defensive_abilities":["electricity discharge (DC 13, 3d6 electricity)"],"dr":"10/magic","immunities":["cold","combat maneuvers","electricity","poison"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to sunlight"],"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":40,"maneuverability":"good"}],"space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"animate dead"},{"type":"lightning bolt","details":"30 ft. line, DC 16, 3d6 electricity, useable every other round"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":4,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":5,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"animate dead"}]}],"strength":11,"dexterity":16,"constitution":12,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":11,"charisma":14,"baseatk":3,"feats":[{"feat":"Ability Focus (lightning bolt)"},{"feat":"Dodge"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":14},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":9},{"skill":"Perception","value":7},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":4},{"skill":"Stealth","value":10,"special":"+14 to move silently, +22 to hide in fog or mist"}],"languages":["Auran","Common"],"sq":[{"type":"gaseous form"}],"environments":["cold hills","cold plains"],"organizations":["solitary","troupe (1-6 zombies [see text])"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature resembles a humanoid formed of fog and mist. The only discernible facial feature is its icy blue eyes.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Animate Dead","kind":"Su","details":"The electrical aura of the fogwarden can animate dead creatures within 20 ft. This is otherwise identical to an animate dead (caster level 4th). The animated creatures resemble zombies (and use their stats) and are under the control of the fogwarden that animated them. They are not undead however, and cannot be turned or rebuked. If the fogwarden is slain or moves more than 20 ft. from a zombie, the animated creature collapses dead and cannot be animated again."},{"type":"Electricity Discharge","kind":"Su","details":"Electricity constantly plays across a fogwarden's form. Any metal object (including metal weapons) that contacts a fogwarden's body takes 3d6 points of electricity damage. Magic items receive a DC 13 Reflex saving throw to reduce the damage by half. Nonmagical items and objects receive no save and automatically take full damage. A creature holding the object or weapon at the time of contact takes 3d6 points of electricity damage as well (DC 13 Reflex save for half)."},{"type":"Gaseous Form","kind":"Ex","details":"The fogwarden's natural form is that of fog or mist. This ability is similar to the gaseous form spell (caster level 8th), except that a fogwarden doesn't lose its supernatural abilities or its lightning bolt ability, and has a fly speed of 40 ft. It is immune to and cannot perform combat maneuvers."},{"type":"Vulnerability to Sunlight","kind":"Ex","details":"Fogwardens shun sunlight. A fogwarden exposed to sunlight is staggered for as long as it remains in the sunlight, and is destroyed utterly after 1 hour of exposure if it cannot escape."}],"description":"The fogwarden is sometimes called the ice apparition, for much like the standard apparition, the fogwarden feeds on the fear of its victims. The fogwarden, however, isn't undead. A fogwarden is usually found inhabiting the coldest and most desolate areas of the world. The fog surrounding it flashes with its life force. These flashes are often mistaken for the will-o'-wisp. Fogwardens favor instilling fear and panic in their opponents to actual combat. In melee, the fogwarden attacks by launching a bolt of lightning at its foes. When a fogwarden is destroyed, it evaporates completely, leaving no trace of its existence.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Fogwarden originally appeared in the Second Edition Monstrous Compendium Annual 4 (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1997) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Forester's Bane","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"plant","init":0,"senses":[{"type":"blindsight","modifier":"30 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":17,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"+8 natural, -1 size","hp":52,"hd":"5d8+30","hdvalue":5,"fort":10,"ref":1,"will":2,"immunities":["plant traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":0,"special":"immobile"}],"melee":"4 leaves +5 touch (grab), 6 stalks +5 (1d4+3)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"snap and saw"}],"strength":17,"dexterity":10,"constitution":22,"wisdom":13,"charisma":9,"baseatk":3,"cmb":7,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":17,"environments":["temperate plains"],"organizations":["solitary","pair"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature resembles a huge, dark green shrub.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Snap and Saw","kind":"Ex","details":"A forester's bane can saw at an opponent, dealing slashing damage, when it makes a successful grapple check. This attack deals 1d4+3 points of slashing damage per stalk. It cannot attack a pinned opponent with any stalk that has already attacked another opponent that round. A forester's bane can only attempt to grapple opponents 1 or more sizes smaller than itself. Because of its four leaves, it can grapple up to four different opponents at one time with a single grapple check. It can also attack a single opponent with more than one leaf, gaining a +2 bonus on its grapple check with each extra leaf (+13 grapple with two leaves, +15 grapple with three leaves, and +17 grapple with all four leaves). Both leaves and stalks each have 10 hit points and can be attacked by making a successful sunder attempt. Attacking a forester's bane's leaf or stalk doesn't provoke an attack of opportunity. If the leaf is currently grappling a target, the forester's bane takes a -4 penalty on its opposed roll to resist the sunder attempt. Severing a leaf or stalk deals no damage to a forester's bane. Attacks that hit a leaf deal half their damage to the monster and half to the trapped victim. Destroyed leaves and stalks grow back in 2d4 weeks if the forester's bane isn't killed."}],"description":"The forester's bane is a huge, immobile, and carnivorous shrub. Closer inspection reveals large, tough leaves radiating from its central stalk.\n\nThese dark green leaves hide six purple serrated stalks inside its body. At the center of this low-growing shrub is a 3-foot diameter yellowish orb from which sprout many small green branches. Each branch has small, sweet smelling (and tasting) berries of various colors growing from it.\n\nWhen a living creature moves near a forester's bane's leaves, it attempts to grab the creature. Trapped creatures are subjected to attacks by several serrated stalks that slash and cut until the opponent escapes. The forester's bane releases a trapped victim when either it or the victim is dead, or the leaf holding the victim is destroyed. The snapper saw can also attack with its stalks without first grappling an opponent.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Forester's Bane originally appeared in the First Edition module S3 Expedition to the Barrier Peaks (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1980) and later in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Four-armed Gargoyle","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"CE","size":"Medium","type":"monstrous humanoid","subtypes":["earth"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":16,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":14,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +4 natural","hp":57,"hd":"6d10+24","hdvalue":6,"fort":6,"ref":7,"will":5,"dr":"10/magic","speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"average"}],"melee":"4 claws +8 (1d6+2), bite +8 (1d6+2),  gore +8 (1d6+2)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","strength":15,"dexterity":14,"constitution":18,"intelligence":6,"wisdom":11,"charisma":7,"baseatk":6,"cmb":8,"cmd":20,"feats":[{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Fly)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":12},{"skill":"Perception","value":9},{"skill":"Stealth","value":11,"special":"+15 stony environs"}],"languages":["Common","Terran"],"sq":[{"type":"freeze"}],"environments":["any land","any aquatic","any underground"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","wing (5-16)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This creature appears to be a hideous and winged humanoid carved of stone. Its ears are oversized and pointed and two large backward-curving horns just from its head above its eyes. Its four arms end in stony claws.","group":"Gargoyle","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","description":"Four-armed gargoyles like their brethren often stand perched indefinitely without moving in an attempt to surprise their opponents.\n\nThey have a great fondness for inflicting pain on their foes. When a four-armed gargoyle has the upper hand in battle, it often draws out the conflict as long as it can in order to deal as much pain and suffering as it can on its foes.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Four-Armed Gargoyle first appeared in the First Edition module S1 Tomb of Horrors (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1978) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Fungus Gargoyle","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"NE","size":"Medium","type":"plant","subtypes":["fungus"],"init":2,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"}],"auras":["sickening aura (10 ft., DC 16, sickened)"],"ac":17,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":15,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +5 natural","hp":59,"hd":"7d8+21 (+7)","hdvalue":7,"fort":8,"ref":4,"will":4,"dr":"10/slashing or piercing","immunities":["plant traits"],"resists":[{"type":"fire","value":5}],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"average"}],"melee":"2 claws +9 (1d8+4)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon"}],"strength":18,"dexterity":14,"constitution":17,"intelligence":6,"wisdom":11,"charisma":7,"baseatk":5,"cmb":9,"cmd":21,"feats":[{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Toughness"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":2},{"skill":"Perception","value":12},{"skill":"Stealth","value":10,"special":"+18 in vegetation"}],"languages":["Common (can't speak)"],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","patch (5-10)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature looks like a winged statue, humanoid in shape, carved from molds, funguses, and mushrooms. Its arms and legs end in clawed hands and ft., and its mouth is lined with fangs carved from the same substances its body is.","group":"Gargoyle","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"Once every 1d4 rounds, a fungus gargoyle can breathe a line of deadly spores to a range of 10 ft. A living creature struck must succeed on a DC 16 Fortitude save or take 1d4 points of Strength damage. Thereafter, the creature must succeed on a DC 16 Fortitude save each minute (10 rounds) or take 1 point of Strength damage. This cycle continues until the creature dies or receives a remove disease spell. A successful DC 20 Heal check or a delay poison spell slows the continuing damage to 1 point per hour. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Sickening Aura","kind":"Su","details":"As a free action, a fungus gargoyle can emanate an aura that smells like rotting vegetable matter in a 10-foot radius. Creatures within the area must succeed on a DC 16 Fortitude save or be sickened for as long as they remain in the area and for 1d4 rounds afterwards. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"Fungus gargoyles are thought to be gargoyles that have been transformed into their current state by an evil cult that pays reverence to various demons of slime, ooze, and fungus. These creatures are often found acting as guardians in temples dedicated to such demons.\n\nUnlike normal plants, fungus gargoyles don't require food or air (they still require water however), but sometimes eat their fallen enemies simply for the sheer pleasure of doing so (usually only evil-aligned fungus gargoyles do this). A typical fungus gargoyle stands about 5 or 6 ft. tall and weighs up to 200 pounds. Though its shape can vary, most resemble ugly winged humanoids.\n\nFungus gargoyles typically ambush their prey, standing motionless until their opponent moves close. The fungus gargoyles then leap to the attack, slashing with their claws. Most fungus gargoyles try to stay airborne during combat rather than fight on the ground.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Fungus Gargoyle originally appeared in the First Edition Fiend Folio (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1981) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Gargoyle Stone Idol","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Medium","type":"construct","init":2,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":20,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":18,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +8 natural","hp":47,"hd":"5d10+20","hdvalue":5,"fort":1,"ref":3,"will":1,"defensive_abilities":["rejuvenation"],"dr":"10/adamantine","immunities":["construct traits (+20 hp)","magic"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"2 claws +9 (1d8+4), bite +9 (1d6+4), gore +9 (1d6+4)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"30-ft. cone, 4d6 fire damage and see below, Reflex DC 14 half, usable every 1d4 rounds"}],"strength":19,"dexterity":14,"wisdom":11,"charisma":7,"baseatk":5,"cmb":9,"cmd":21,"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":2,"special":"+12 jumping"}],"sq":[{"type":"site bound"}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","pair"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This crouching horned and winged automaton appears to be carved from stone.","group":"Stone Idol","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Immunity to Magic","kind":"Ex","details":"A stone idol is immune to any spell or spell-like ability that allows spell resistance. In addition, certain spells and effects function differently against the creature, as noted below. A transmute rock to mud spell slows a stone idol (as the slow spell) for 2d6 rounds, with no saving throw, while transmute mud to rock heals all of its lost hit points. A stone to flesh spell doesn't actually change the stone idol's structure but negates its damage reduction and immunity to magic for 1 full round. A disintegrate spell deals +50% damage to a stone idol. A chaos hammer, holy smite, order's wrath, or unholy blight spell deals 1d4 points of damage per two caster levels to a stone idol if the creator's alignment matches one of the aforementioned spells."},{"type":"Rejuvenation","kind":"Su","details":"Unless a stone idol's main body is shattered into small fragments and scattered to the winds, the creature reforms itself at full strength in 1d4+2 days."},{"type":"Site Bound","kind":"Ex","details":"A stone idol cannot travel more than 200 ft. from a central point designated by its creator. Once this point is selected, it can never be changed. A stone idol taken outside the area ceases functioning until it is brought back into the area."},{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"The stone gargoyle's breath weapon is a cone of superheated steam and water. Creatures of an alignment opposite that of the cleric that created the stone gargoyle are also sickened 1d4+3 rounds if they fail their save. The save DC is Constitution-based and includes a +2 racial bonus."}],"description":"Stone gargoyles stand 7 ft. tall and weigh about 600 pounds. Though they have wings, they cannot fly. They can give the appearance of flight by leaping from high places and flapping their stone wings.\n\nConstruction\n\nA stone gargoyle's body is chiseled from a single block of hard stone, such as granite, weighing at least 2,000 pounds. The stone must be of exceptional quality, and costs 3,000 gp.\n\nSTONE GARGOYLE\n\nCL 12th; Price 39,000 gp\n\nRequirements Craft Construct, antimagic field, geas/ quest, limited wish, bless water or curse water, creator must be caster level 12th; Skill Craft (sculpting) or Craft (stonemasonry) DC 17; Cost 21,000 gp","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Geruzou Demon","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"CE","size":"Small","type":"outsider","subtypes":["chaotic","demon","evil","extraplanar"],"init":2,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":23,"ac_touch":17,"ac_flat_footed":21,"ac_mods":"+4 deflection, +2 Dex, +6 natural, +1 size","hp":39,"hd":"6d10+6","hdvalue":6,"fort":3,"ref":7,"will":4,"defensive_abilities":["slime armor"],"dr":"10/cold iron or good","immunities":["electricity","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":16,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":50,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"2 claws +10 (1d4+1), bite +10 (1d6+1)","ranged":"ranged touch +9 (spit slime)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"whisper of madness"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":8,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":9,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"cause fear"},{"spell":"darkness"},{"spell":"detect good"},{"spell":"detect thoughts"},{"spell":"invisibility","details":"self only"},{"spell":"mirror image"},{"spell":"scare"},{"spell":"stinking cloud"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"summon","details":"level 3, 1 geruzou 35%"}]}],"strength":12,"dexterity":15,"constitution":12,"intelligence":8,"wisdom":8,"charisma":10,"baseatk":6,"cmb":6,"cmd":22,"feats":[{"feat":"Weapon Finesse"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claw)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":11},{"skill":"Fly","value":17},{"skill":"Perception","value":12},{"skill":"Stealth","value":15},{"skill":"Survival","value":8}],"languages":["Abyssal","common","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Abyss)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This humanoid appears to stand nearly 4 ft. tall and has a horse-like head with downward-curving horns jutting from its head. Its mouth is filled with long, sharp teeth and its hands and ft. end in sharpened claws. A pair of large, membranous wings jut from its back and its flesh is sickly gray and appears to be covered with a thick layer of slimy mucus.","group":"Demon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Slime Armor","kind":"Ex","details":"The slime excreted by a geruzou grants it a +4 deflection bonus to AC. This bonus is already included in the statistics block."},{"type":"Spit Slime","kind":"Ex","details":"Once every 1d4 rounds as a standard action, a geruzou can spit a stream of slimy goo in a 20-foot line (no range increment). This requires a successful ranged touch attack. A creature hit is slowed (as the slow spell, caster level 6th) for 6 rounds if it fails a DC 14 Fortitude save. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"Geruzou are sometimes called slime demons because their leathery skin constantly drips and oozes thick, jelly-like mucus. Like their brethren, they are fierce combatants and are often employed as hunters and trackers by greater demons. The typical geruzou stands nearly 4 ft. tall and weighs about 140 pounds.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Giant Assassin Bug","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Medium","type":"vermin","init":3,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":17,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":14,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +4 natural","hp":67,"hd":"9d8+27","hdvalue":9,"fort":9,"ref":6,"will":1,"immunities":["mind-affecting effects","vermin traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"climb","speed":20},{"type":"fly","speed":50,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"2 claws +8 (1d6+2), bite +8 (1d8+2 plus liquefy organs)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"liquefy organs"}],"strength":14,"dexterity":17,"constitution":16,"wisdom":12,"charisma":9,"baseatk":6,"cmb":4,"cmd":16,"cmd_special":"+8 vs. trip","skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":14},{"skill":"Fly","value":7}],"sq":[{"type":"sticky pads"}],"environments":["temperate forests"],"organizations":["solitary","cluster (2-5)","colony (6-11)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This large insect has a narrow head ending in a segmented beak or proboscis.  The creature's carapace is dull brownish-black and its front jackknife legs are covered in thousands of small hairs. Two long segmented antennae jut from its head.","group":"Assassin Bug","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Liquefy Organs","kind":"Ex","details":": An assassin bug that has pinned a foe can inject it with a corrosive poison that liquefies the prey's insides, dealing 1d6 points of Constitution damage each round the hold is maintained. At Constitution 0, a creature dies as its bones and internal organs are liquefied. Creatures without internal organs or Constitution scores are immune to the ability damaging effects of the assassin bug's liquefy organs attack."},{"type":"Sticky Pads","kind":"Ex","details":": An assassin bug's forelegs are covered in thousands of tiny hairs that secrete a sticky residue aiding the creature in climbing as well as securing its prey. An assassin bug has a +4 racial bonus on Climb checks and on grapple checks (already figured into its statistics block)."}],"description":"Assassin bugs are predatory insects that feed on the blood and tissue of living creatures. Actively hunting or passively waiting for its prey, an assassin bug is a formidable killing machine that has few enemies.\n\nAssassin bugs are communal creatures and nests of up to 20 or so are not unheard of. Most nests contain at least one female of mating age and during mating season the female deposits a sticky clutch of eggs (2d4) in cracks or crevices in the forest floor. The eggs hatch within two weeks and newborn assassin bugs look exactly like their adult counterparts (other than being smaller). An assassin bug goes through several growth stages before finally reaching adult stage within one year.\n\nAn assassin bug stands 5 ft. tall. Its body is segmented and almost always dull brownish black (though red and black or even yellowish-brown assassin bugs have been reported). Its front curved legs (called jackknife legs) are black and covered in tiny hairs that aid it in climbing as well as capturing its prey. An assassin bug has two pairs of wings that it keeps folded against its back when not using them to fly.\n\nDepending on the disposition of the assassin bug, it is either an opportunistic ambush hunter that lies in wait for its prey to come close, or it actively seeks out its food. Regardless, when a victim is within range, the assassin bug leaps to the attack, attempting to grapple and pins its prey so it can inject it with its organ-dissolving saliva. A victim that dies is kept in the assassin bug's lair for several weeks and feasted upon by it and any others in the nest, each taking a turn drinking the liquefied internals of the victim.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Giant Barracuda","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"animal","subtypes":["aquatic"],"init":1,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":18,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +8 natural, -1 size","hp":59,"hd":"7d8+21 (+7)","hdvalue":7,"fort":8,"ref":6,"will":3,"speed":[{"type":"swim","speed":50}],"melee":"bite +10 (1d8+7/19-20)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","strength":20,"dexterity":13,"constitution":17,"intelligence":1,"wisdom":12,"charisma":2,"baseatk":5,"cmb":11,"cmd":22,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)","type":"bonus"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":13},{"skill":"Swim","value":17}],"environments":["any aquatic"],"organizations":["pair","pack (2-5)","school (6-11)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This fish is long and bluish gray fading to mottled silver near it tail. It has an oversized jaw full of sharp teeth.","group":"Barracuda","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","description":"The barracuda is a predatory fish that averages about two ft. long and weighs 10-15 pounds. Its body is bluish-gray near the front changing to silver mottled with black spots in the rear. Its mouth is filled with razor-sharp teeth. Medium barracudas are about six ft. long and weigh 30-45 pounds. Large barracudas are about ten ft. long and weigh 50-80 pounds.\n\nThe barracuda strikes quickly in combat. Slain prey is devoured immediately.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Queen Giant Bumblebee","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"vermin","init":2,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":18,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":16,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +7 natural, -1 size","hp":52,"hd":"8d8+16","hdvalue":8,"fort":8,"ref":4,"will":3,"immunities":["mind-affecting effects"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"sting +9 (2d6+7 plus poison)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","strength":20,"dexterity":14,"constitution":14,"wisdom":13,"charisma":11,"baseatk":5,"cmb":11,"cmd":23,"cmd_special":"+9 vs. trip","skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":4},{"skill":"Perception","value":5},{"skill":"Survival","value":1,"special":"+5 to keep from getting lost"}],"environments":["temperate forests","temperate plains"],"organizations":["solitary","buzz (2-5)","hive (11-20)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This is a giant-sized bumblebee, much larger than its normal sized counterpart.","group":"Bumblebee","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Sting-injury; save Fortitude DC 16; frequency; 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d4 Con; cure 1 save. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"Giant bumblebees generally behave like their much smaller relatives, building underground nests and burrows. Workers collect nectar and pollen and build or repair the burrow while the queen creates a brood chamber where she lays her eggs. The queen lays her eggs over the entire summer months. In late summer and early autumn, the eggs hatch, forming new drones and queens. Both drones and queens leave the nest to mate with other bumblebees. A giant bumblebee is about 8 ft. long with a black body striped with yellow bands. Giant bumblebees are generally passive creatures. If threatened however, or if their nest is disturbed, they respond by stinging their opponents.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Giant Forest Lizard","cr":5,"xp":1600,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"animal","init":6,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":19,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +8 natural, -1 size","hp":68,"hd":"8d8+32","hdvalue":8,"fort":12,"ref":8,"will":3,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"climb","speed":20}],"melee":"bite +12 (2d6+9 plus poison)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","strength":23,"dexterity":15,"constitution":19,"intelligence":2,"wisdom":12,"charisma":10,"baseatk":6,"cmb":13,"cmd":25,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":6,"special":"+14 jumping"},{"skill":"Climb","value":18},{"skill":"Perception","value":11},{"skill":"Stealth","value":3,"special":"+7 in undergrowth"}],"sq":[{"type":"powerful leaper"}],"environments":["temperate forests"],"organizations":["solitary","pack (2-5)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This giant lizard has brown and green markings on its body, a long, thick tail, and a blunt snout that opens to reveal a mouth full of strong, thick teeth.","group":"Lizard","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"Bite-injury; save DC 18 Fort; frequency 1/round for 6 rounds; effect 1d4 Dexterity damage; cure 2 saves. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Powerful Leaper","kind":"Ex","details":"A giant forest lizard uses its Strength to modify Acrobatics checks made to jump, and it has a +8 racial bonus on Acrobatics checks made to jump."}],"description":"Giant forest lizards are carnivorous animals that dwell in overgrown forests, making their lairs in hidden caves and passages. These creatures are highly territorial, nocturnal and spend most of the day sleeping in their lair or sunning themselves on large tree limbs where the sun breaks through the treetops. Giant forest lizards dine on other forest animals, consuming almost anything they find. When food is scarce, they scavenge as well. A typical giant forest lizard's territory covers several square miles.\n\nA giant forest lizard is 9 ft. long and weighs nearly 2,000 pounds. Its coloration and markings are browns and greens, allowing it to adapt and hide in the forests. These creatures mate but once a year with the female depositing up to four eggs in the lair. Eggs hatch within 3 months and young reach maturity within 10 months. Forest lizards can live to be 20 years old.\n\nWhen hunting, a giant forest lizard perches within the trees on strong, overhanging limbs. When potential prey passes beneath it, it drops to the ground and attacks. Prey that is killed is carried back to its lair and eaten or saved for later consumption. In combat, or when warning other creatures that have entered its territory, the giant forest lizard vocalizes, emitting a deep, rolling hissing sound.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""}];
